<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE topic PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA Topic//EN" "topic.dtd">
<topic id="git-addon-cloning-a-repository">
  <title>Clone a Repository</title>
  
  <prolog>
    <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <indexterm>Git Client add-on<indexterm>cloning repositories</indexterm></indexterm>
        <indexterm>Git Client add-on<indexterm>working copies</indexterm></indexterm>
      </keywords>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
  <body>
    <p id="p_egp_p3y_kpb">In the <xref
        href="git-addon-git-staging-view-interface.dita#git-addon-git-staging-view-interface"
          ><uicontrol>Git Staging</uicontrol> view</xref> toolbar, open the <xref
        href="git-addon-git-staging-view-interface.dita#git-addon-git-staging-view-interface/section_git_staging_ellipsis_menu"
            ><uicontrol><image href="../img/Ellipsis18.png"/>Ellipsis</uicontrol> menu</xref>, use
      the <uicontrol><image href="../img/Add16.png" id="image_urd_gsd_s2c"/>Clone
        repository</uicontrol> action, and provide the following:<ul id="ul_fgp_p3y_kpb">
        <li id="li_ggp_p3y_kpb"><uicontrol>Repository URL</uicontrol> - The URL of the remote
          repository to clone.</li>
        <li id="li_hgp_p3y_kpb"><uicontrol>Checkout branch</uicontrol> - The branch to check out from
          the cloned repository. If you do not specify a branch, the default branch is cloned.</li>
        <li id="li_igp_p3y_kpb"><uicontrol>Destination path</uicontrol> - The local path where the
          repository is cloned. When you enter a repository URL, the Git Client suggests a folder
          with the same name as the repository.</li>
      </ul></p>
    <p>
      <fig id="fig_git_clone_repository_dialog">
        <title>Clone Repository Dialog Box</title>
        <image href="../img/git-addon/dialogs/clone_repository.png" placement="inline"
          id="image_git_clone_repository_dialog"/>
      </fig>
    </p>
    <p id="p_jgp_p3y_kpb">After the repository is cloned, it is automatically set as the current
      working copy.</p>
  </body>
</topic>
